Subject: [PATCH] modesetting: use 64-bit constants for the identity CTM

An unsigned long is only 32 bits on ARM32. Shifting 1UL by 32 bits does
not produce the required S31.32 fixed-point representation of one. The
resulting invalid identity matrix can turn all output colours black when
the kernel exposes the CTM property.

Use unsigned long long constants, as the identity comparison already does.

Upstream-Status: Backport [https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/xorg/xserver/-/commit/69beb656539d5f9f82ec501f42245d0f43b709d8]

diff --git a/hw/xfree86/drivers/modesetting/drmmode_display.c b/hw/xfree86/drivers/modesetting/drmmode_display.c
--- a/hw/xfree86/drivers/modesetting/drmmode_display.c
+++ b/hw/xfree86/drivers/modesetting/drmmode_display.c
@@ -63,9 +63,9 @@
                                               void *pPixData);
 
 static const struct drm_color_ctm ctm_identity = { {
-    1UL << 32, 0, 0,
-    0, 1UL << 32, 0,
-    0, 0, 1UL << 32
+    1ULL << 32, 0, 0,
+    0, 1ULL << 32, 0,
+    0, 0, 1ULL << 32
 } };
 
 static Bool ctm_is_identity(const struct drm_color_ctm *ctm)
